    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0504" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100K77/81.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have just been officially advised that the Dominican Minister at Washington has
                    informed the Government of the official note of the Department announcing the
                    proposed visit of Mr. Knox. The Minister for Foreign Affairs said to me: “This
                    pleasing news has been received by my Government with real satisfaction, and I
                    can assure your excellency that such an illustrious visitor will receive the
                    warmest of welcome in Dominican territory.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
